  "id": "meatyourmaker",
  "neon": "#ff3e4a",
  "note": "MEAT YOUR MAKER — the butcher at the south end of Ironside Street.\n\n⚠ THE CHILLER IS ON THE ROOF AND IT IS HALF THE BUILDING. A butcher is a cold room with a counter\nin front of it, so the plant is not decoration hung on a shop — it is the larger half, and putting\nit up where it can be seen from the street is what makes the shop read as a butcher rather than as\na red-painted unit.\n\n⚠ THE DADO IS A SEPARATE BAND AND NOT A PAINTED LINE. Every butcher's shop that has ever existed is\ntiled to shoulder height, because that is the part you wash down. A band of tile under a brick\nshaft costs one mass segment and is the difference between this trade and any other on the street.\n\n⚠ AND THE RAIL COMES OUT UNDER THE CANOPY. The one thing a passer-by actually sees a butcher use.",
  "pal": "ty_butcher",
